<h1>Elgie R. Sims, Jr.</h1>
<p>Illinois Senate, 17th District, on the Chicago ballot November 3, 2026. Party: Democratic. Incumbent.</p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>As Senate Majority Caucus Appropriations Leader he describes his budget priorities as educating young people, expanding good-paying job opportunities, and keeping communities safe; his recent legislative work has focused on criminal justice measures such as the Clean Slate Act and compensation for the wrongfully incarcerated, and on economic development in the district.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Attorney who served in the Illinois House for the 34th District from 2012 to 2018 and earlier worked as a budget analyst and Appropriations Director for Senate President Emil Jones Jr.</p>
